    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1478">

                <pb facs="0960" n="844" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg844"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.41/99</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Carothers to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 20, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Resolutions adopted at mass meeting demanding investigation Benton matter. Have
                    not received copy of proceedings but expect them early in morning. It appears to
                    me that Benton went to Juarez seeking trouble. His cousin and business associate
                    William Benton told me in Cobb’s presence that he had urged Benton not to go,
                    that he would get into trouble, but he insisted stating he was going to tell him
                    what he thought of him. He secured a card from Alfredo Farias which secured him
                    admittance to Villa’s room. He at once commenced to rail at Villa and heated
                    discussion resulted. Insults were passed by both, a struggle ensued but they
                    were separated by Andres L. Farias. Villa ordered Benton taken to guardhouse.
                    Some doubt exists as to after procedure and execution which will be explained in
                    alleged military proceedings.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">G. C. Carothers</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
